        "factor": "Altman Z-score distress signal",
        "direction": "up",
        "magnitude": "strong",
        "rationale": "Frontier's Z-score around 0.37–0.38 places it in the distress zone; within the Altman framework, distressed-zone firms have historically high bankruptcy probabilities within two years."
      },
      {
        "factor": "Near-term debt maturities",
        "direction": "up",
        "magnitude": "moderate",
        "rationale": "Debt maturities of roughly $209M in 2025 remainder and $120M in 2026 increase refinancing risk despite current liquidity."
      },
      {
        "factor": "Industry-wide distress environment",
        "direction": "up",
        "magnitude": "moderate",
        "rationale": "Rising corporate distress and higher bankruptcy activity in 2025–2026 raise baseline risk for leveraged airlines."
      },
      {
        "factor": "Liquidity cushion and near-term liquidity",
        "direction": "down",
        "magnitude": "moderate",
        "rationale": "Substantial liquidity (around $889M) including an undrawn revolver reduces near-term bankruptcy risk and provides runway."
      },
      {
        "factor": "Spirit merger failure reduces rescue options",
        "direction": "up",
        "magnitude": "moderate",
        "rationale": "Loss of potential strategic rescue financing via Spirit increases distress risk for Frontier if other relief options do not emerge."
      }
    ],
    "synthesis_rationale": "The posterior probability reflects a calibration that heavily weighs the persistent distress signals (Z-score) and industry risk, moderated by Frontier's liquidity cushion and lack of an imminent filing as of early 2026. The raw estimate was near 90%, and correlation among distress and liquidity factors was accounted for, yielding a final calibrated probability of 89% with an uncertainty band."
  }
}

